{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1679935,"ns":0,"title":"Electric power quality","extract":"Electric power quality is the degree to which the voltage, frequency, and waveform of a power supply system conform to established specifications.  Good power quality can be defined as a steady supply voltage that stays within the prescribed range, steady AC frequency close to the rated value, and smooth voltage curve waveform (which resembles a sine wave).","description":"Measurement of power meeting specifications","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}